Below is a **step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, tooling recommendations, and best‑practice tips.  

---

## 1️⃣  Define the Scope & Gather Requirements

| What you need | Why it matters |
|---------------|----------------|
| **Core features** (catalog, search, filters, cart, checkout, user auth, reviews, wishlist) | Keeps the project focused |
| **Target devices** (desktop, tablet, mobile) | Drives responsive design |
| **Performance goals** (first paint < 1 s, LCP < 2 s) | SEO & UX |
| **Accessibility** (WCAG 2.1 AA) | Inclusive design |
| **SEO** (structured data, sitemap, robots.txt) | Organic traffic |
| **Analytics** (GA4, Mixpanel) | Data‑driven decisions |
| **Payment gateway** (Stripe, PayPal, Braintree) | Checkout flow |
| **Hosting** (Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify, Cloudflare Pages) | Deployment strategy |
| **CI/CD** (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) | Automation |

> **Tip:** Create a *feature backlog* in a tool like Jira or Trello. Prioritize by business value.

---

## 2️⃣  Choose the Tech Stack

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG + ISR) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux, Zustand, Recoil, React‑Query | **React‑Query** for server state + **Zustand** for UI state |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS, Material‑UI, Chakra‑UI, Ant Design | **Tailwind + Headless UI** (utility‑first + accessible components) |
| **Type system** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (type safety, IDE support) |
| **API** | REST, GraphQL | **REST** (simpler for small projects) or **GraphQL** if you need flexible queries |
| **Testing** | Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress | **Jest + RTL** for unit tests, **Cypress** for E2E |
| **Linting/Formatting** | ESLint, Prettier | **ESLint + Prettier** with Airbnb config |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI | **GitHub Actions** (free for public repos) |
| **Deployment** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (Next.js first‑class support) |
| **Analytics** | GA4, Plausible, Mixpanel | **GA4** + **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly) |
| **Payment** | Stripe Elements, PayPal SDK | **Stripe Elements** (modern, PCI‑compliant) |
| **Image CDN** | Cloudinary, Imgix, Vercel Image Optimization | **Vercel Image** (auto‑optimisation) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Server‑Side Rendering (SSR) → instant content for crawlers  
> • Static Site Generation (SSG) → fast pages for catalog  
> • Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) → update product pages without rebuild  
> • Built‑in API routes → simple backend for cart, checkout, etc.

---

## 3️⃣  Wireframe & Design System

1. **Sketch the user journey** (home → product → cart → checkout).  
2. Use **Figma** or **Adobe XD** to create high‑fidelity mockups.  
3. Build a **design system** (colors, typography, spacing, components).  
4. Export design tokens (JSON) and import into Tailwind config.  

```js
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        primary: '#1D4ED8',
        secondary: '#F59E0B',
        accent: '#10B981',
      },
      spacing: {
        18: '4.5rem',
        22: '5.5rem',
      },
    },
  },
};
```

---

## 4️⃣  Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest my-ecommerce --typescript
cd my-ecommerce
npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

Add Tailwind to `globals.css`:

```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
```

Create a **folder structure**:

```
/components   # UI components
/pages        # Next.js pages
/pages/api    # API routes
/lib          # utilities (fetch, auth, cart)
/store        # Zustand stores
/styles       # Tailwind overrides
/hooks        # custom hooks
/tests        # Jest + RTL tests
```

---

## 5️⃣  Core Components & Pages

### 5.1  Product Card (React + Tailwind)

```tsx
// components/ProductCard.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import Image from 'next/image';

type Product = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  imageUrl: string;
};

export const ProductCard: React.FC<{ product: Product }> = ({ product }) => (
  <Link href={`/product/${product.id}`}>
    <a className="block border rounded-lg overflow-hidden hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
      <div className="relative w-full h-48">
        <Image src={product.imageUrl} alt={product.title} layout="fill" objectFit="cover" />
      </div>
      <div className="p-4">
        <h3 className="font-semibold text-lg truncate">{product.title}</h3>
        <p className="text-primary font-bold mt-2">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
      </div>
    </a>
  </Link>
);
```

### 5.2  Home Page (SSG)

```tsx
// pages/index.tsx
import { GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { ProductCard } from '../components/ProductCard';

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/products');
  const products = await res.json();
  return { props: { products }, revalidate: 60 }; // ISR
};

export default function Home({ products }: { products: any[] }) {
  return (
    <main className="container mx-auto py-8">
      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Shop</h1>
      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        {products.map((p) => (
          <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </main>
  );
}
```

### 5.3  Cart Context (Zustand)

```ts
// store/cart.ts
import create from 'zustand';

type CartItem = {
  id: string;
  quantity: number;
};

type CartState = {
  items: CartItem[];
  addItem: (id: string) => void;
  removeItem: (id: string) => void;
  clearCart: () => void;
};

export const useCart = create<CartState>((set) => ({
  items: [],
  addItem: (id) =>
    set((state) => ({
      items: [...state.items, { id, quantity: 1 }],
    })),
  removeItem: (id) =>
    set((state) => ({
      items: state.items.filter((i) => i.id !== id),
    })),
  clearCart: () => set({ items: [] }),
}));
```

### 5.4  Checkout Page (Stripe Elements)

```tsx
// pages/checkout.tsx
import { loadStripe } from '@stripe/stripe-js';
import { Elements } from '@stripe/react-stripe-js';
import CheckoutForm from '../components/CheckoutForm';

const stripePromise = loadStripe(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY!);

export default function Checkout() {
  return (
    <Elements stripe={stripePromise}>
      <CheckoutForm />
    </Elements>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// components/CheckoutForm.tsx
import { CardElement, useStripe, useElements } from '@stripe/react-stripe-js';
import { useState } from 'react';

export default function CheckoutForm() {
  const stripe = useStripe();
  const elements = useElements();
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

  const handleSubmit = async (e: React.FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (!stripe || !elements) return;
    setLoading(true);

    const { error, paymentMethod } = await stripe.createPaymentMethod({
      type: 'card',
      card: elements.getElement(CardElement)!,
    });

    if (error) {
      console.error(error);
      setLoading(false);
      return;
    }

    // Call your backend to create a PaymentIntent
    const res = await fetch('/api/checkout', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ paymentMethodId: paymentMethod!.id }),
    });

    const data = await res.json();
    if (data.error) {
      console.error(data.error);
      setLoading(false);
      return;
    }

    // Confirm the payment
    const confirmRes = await stripe.confirmCardPayment(data.clientSecret);
    if (confirmRes.error) {
      console.error(confirmRes.error);
    } else {
      alert('Payment successful!');
    }
    setLoading(false);
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className="max-w-md mx-auto p-4 border rounded">
      <CardElement className="border p-2 rounded mb-4" />
      <button
        type="submit"
        disabled={!stripe || loading}
        className="w-full bg-primary text-white py-2 rounded disabled:opacity-50"
      >
        {loading ? 'Processing…' : 'Pay'}
      </button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

---

## 6️⃣  API Routes (Next.js)

```ts
// pages/api/checkout.ts
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import Stripe from 'stripe';

const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, {
  apiVersion: '2023-10-16',
});

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  if (req.method !== 'POST') return res.status(405).end();

  const { paymentMethodId } = req.body;

  try {
    const paymentIntent = await stripe.paymentIntents.create({
      amount: 9999, // $99.99
      currency: 'usd',
      payment_method: paymentMethodId,
      confirmation_method: 'manual',
      confirm: true,
    });

    res.status(200).json({ clientSecret: paymentIntent.client_secret });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

